      "content": "Burning urination and lower belly pressure, you say? Sounds like a classic UTI. While I understand your hesitation towards antibiotics, I must stress that self-treatment with oregano oil or high doses of cranberry extract is not a guaranteed solution. These methods may not be potent enough to combat the infection effectively. I strongly recommend you consider a more reliable treatment to avoid complications. However, if you're set on trying natural remedies, start with a moderate dose of cranberry extract and monitor your symptoms closely. But remember, if things don't improve, it's time to reconsider your options. Stay healthy!",
